text:
maria: Quick sync — multiple onboarding reports where the sample app shows raw 500/502 HTML blobs to users. We need a consistent error contract across SDKs so apps show friendly messages instead of raw dumps.
aj: +1. Also, don't treat "retryable" as only 5xx. 429 needs retry_after semantics.
devon: Current JS SDK throws plain Error with body string; Go returns status + raw body; Python inconsistent. Parity would reduce support friction.
kevin: Draft canonical shape idea:
```json
{
  "error": {
    "type": "auth|rate_limit|client|server",
    "code": "string_enum",
    "status": 401,
    "message": "short human-friendly message",
    "retryable": "true|false",
    "retry_after": "seconds|null",
    "hint": "short remediation hint (optional)"
  }
}
```
emma: `hint` is great for onboarding (e.g., "rotate key via Console -> API"). `code` must be stable enums; `message` non-sensitive.
maria: For opaque HTML/legacy bodies, map to `{ type: 'server', code: 'unknown_server_error', message: 'Internal server error', retryable: true }` and send raw blob to internal logs only.
aj: 401 -> `unauthorized` (token missing/expired) retryable=false; 403 -> permission denied retryable=false; 429 -> `rate_limited` retryable=true with retry_after.
devon: Streaming: when outputs are partial and then fail, include `stream_status: 'partial'` and attach `error` at stream end to keep shapes consistent.
kevin: SDK implement plan: JS -> RedwoodError subclass with fields (type, code, status, retryAfter, hint); Go -> typed error struct + helpers `IsRetryable(err)` and `Code(err)`; Python -> exception class with attributes and `__str__` returning message.
emma: Update sample app quickstart to include snippet: `if (err.retryable) { showRetryCTA() } else { surfaceHint(err.hint) }` and show concrete UX patterns.
maria: Example JS snippet for quickstart:
```js
try {
  await client.generate(...);
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'rate_limited') {
    setTimeout(() => retry(), (err.retryAfter || 5) * 1000);
  } else {
    showUserMessage(err.message || 'Something went wrong');
    if (err.hint) showHint(err.hint);
  }
}
```
aj: ops-bot, add tracing/datadog tag `redwood.error.code`?
ops-bot: ✅ created tag `redwood.error.code` for traces/logs.
kevin: Open question: include `details` in wire responses? Lean NO — keep debug details in internal logs to avoid leaking internal state.
maria: Agreed. Also will draft mapping table doc for SDK maintainers: HTTP -> type/code/retryable.
devon: Action items:
1) kevin: write RFC with JSON shape + HTTP mapping table (401/403/429/5xx) — due EOD Fri.
2) aj: update JS sampleapp + README with error handling snippets.
3) emma: add error parity checks to onboarding checklist.
4) maria: Console UX doc to prevent raw bodies surfacing and to show hints.
maria: I'll open RFC and a small PR to sampleapp with the JS snippet, will ping #devex when it's up. :thumbsup:
